===Rewards===
[[File:Completed daily challenge icon.png|left]]
After completing a daily challenge, players can open the Challenges interface and click the "Claim Rewards" button. Members will be awarded experience equal to that of a [[large XP lamp]] in the skill related to the challenge, whereas free-to-play players will only get 75% of the experience.

For combat which has multiple skills, players will be given a [[Challenge XP Lamp]] to choose which experience: Constitution, Magic, Ranged, Attack, Defence, Strength, or Necromancy.

Experience to be received is determined by the level when the challenge was assigned, not when it is completed. The experience earned does not take into account the skill's virtual level. The following tables show the experience received from completing a challenge for any given skill level:
<tabber>
Members=
{{LampXP|cols=3|multiplier=4}}
|-|
Free-to-play=
{{LampXP|cols=3|multiplier=3}}
</tabber>

Players can also talk to [[Challenge Mistress Fara]] in [[Burthorpe]] just south of the bank chest, [[Challenge Mistress Rashida]] in the centre of the [[Menaphos]] Plaza near the [[Menaphos lodestone|lodestone]], or [[Challenge Mistress Heriau]] in the [[Max Guild]] to receive the reward.

The reward experience amount is calculated at the moment when the challenge is received, not when completed or claimed. If a member's first login of the day is to a free-to-play world and they receive a challenge in a members' skill, the reward will be limited to the maximum F2P level in that skill.

Players will not receive a reward for a completed challenge if it is allowed to expire before the reward is claimed.

===Influencing assigned daily challenges===
By talking to [[Challenge Mistress Fara]], [[Challenge Mistress Rashida|Rashida]], or [[Challenge Mistress Heriau|Heriau]], players may choose to block receiving new challenges in any skills that they have achieved [[skill mastery]] in. Non-members may block members' skills at level 5 (with the exception of 20 for [[Archaeology]]). Additionally, all challenges in combat skills can be completely disabled if players do not wish to gain combat experience, even if the combat skills are not maxed.

Each skill has its own toggle, so players can choose to block some skills while keeping others assignable. Blocking a skill will not remove challenges for that skill that have already been assigned. Members can take advantage of the level 5 (or 20) "max" in free-to-play to block out challenges from certain members' only skills. This is done by logging into a free-to-play world before reset and blocking the undesired members' skill. After 00:00 in game time, players must log back in to a free-to-play world to receive challenges with the new restrictions. Logging back into a members' world will unblock challenges for all skills not at 99.

[[File:Challenge max toggle interface.png|frame|center|The challenge toggle interface. Blockable (i.e. maxed) skills are outlined in silver, unblockable (i.e. not maxed) skills are outlined in gold. Currently blocked skills are crossed out.]]

If one or two challenges are toggled on, duplicates of unblocked challenges will be rolled. If no challenges are toggled on, challenges won't be given at all.

[[File:Challenge system banner.png|center]]

==Returner Challenges==
Returner challenges were added on [[20 March]] [[2023]], and are made available to players who return to the game after having been away for a time. These returner challenges are available until all 7 Returner Reward Chests have been claimed, or until 20 days have passed since the player first logged in. Returner challenges are not random, but are instead given out in a fixed order. Completed challenges are replaced by new ones every day at 00:00 in game time, while incomplete challenges are not affected.

