Lucky challenges were [[members]]-only rare daily events that could occur while completing activities in game. These challenges could be gained from a range of actions including completing a quest, sending out a voyage in [[Player-Owned Port]]s, or training a skill. It was possible to receive a lucky challenge for a skill even if it has been toggled off by speaking to [[Challenge Mistress Fara]] or [[Heriau]] after achieving level 99 in that skill. If a lucky challenge was received, the player will be notified by a pop-up interface in-game (see an example picture on the right). This interface will contain details of what the challenge requires the player to do. Additionally a message will be displayed in the player's chatbox notifying them that they have received a lucky challenge, for example:

{{RSFont|You've been given a Lucky Challenge: Magic Logs 0/30<br />
Check the Challenges interface to find out more information.|color=#ee7600}}

Only one lucky challenge could be received daily (the day begins at 00:00 UTC). It could take some hours of activity to get one, so an active player can enjoy lucky challenges every day. A lucky challenge had a limited duration of 24 hours. The player could have at most one lucky challenge at once. It was possible, in the span of one day, to complete (and hand in) a lucky challenge of the previous day, and then receive a new lucky challenge.

Lucky challenge would appear in the list of daily challenges in the Challenges tab of the [[Interface#Adventures|Adventures]] interface, but could be distinguished from them by the clover icon, [[File:Lucky Challenge icon.png]] or [[File:Completed Lucky Challenge icon.png]], instead of the star, by duration being measured in hours instead of days, and by the prefix "Lucky Challenge:" in the challenge name. Lucky challenges could not be rerolled nor extended. 

Like daily challenges, completed lucky challenges could be handed in to the challenge mistresses. For this, the player will be rewarded with experience in the relevant skill; the same amount of experience that would be given for a completed daily challenge. Unlike daily challenges, lucky challenges did not award the player with a key for Treasure Hunter (until the removal of Treasure Hunter). It was possible to do daily challenge and lucky challenge at the same time.

