==Trivia==
* The Challenge System was actually only partially available to free players in that they can still be assigned challenges in members' skills, which they aren't permitted to do or hand in. However, in an update on [[22 August]] [[2016]], this was changed so that free players can no longer receive Daily Challenges in members' skills. Daily Challenges in members skills were once again made available to free players in December [[2017]], but an update in January [[2018]] allowed free players to disable such challenges if they have reached the level 5 cap.
* Previously, it was possible (and even likely) for free players to receive members-only items as rewards from challenge mystery bags. Fortunately, free players were now able to sell members items. Alternatively, free players can simply bank members' items, as they will not take up free-to-play bank space. With the removal of challenge mystery bags, this no longer occurs.
* If a completed challenge expires before a log in, the message that you have a complete challenge to hand in will still be displayed.
* Prior the [[Update:Leagues: CATALYST Out today! - This Week In RuneScape|Leagues update]] from [[15 September]] [[2025]], cooking several kinds of raw meat and fish counted towards the Cooking challenge that no longer do. It is unknown if this is intentional.
* Even after the weekly rewards were removed with [[DailyScape Overhaul]] update, the login message about broken weekly progress streaks remained.

